,title,link,text,language,family
0,Djabugay - Wikipedia,https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Djabugay,"The Djabugay people (also known as Djabuganydji or Tjapukai) are a group of Aboriginal Australian people who are the original inhabitants of mountains, gorges, lands and waters of a richly forested part of the Great Dividing Range including the Barron Gorge and surrounding areas within the Wet Tropics of Queensland.",Djabugay,Australian
1,Australian Aboriginal Music And Dance - CulturallyOurs,https://culturallyours.com/podcast/australian-aboriginal-people-music-and-dance/,"In this espiode learn the culture of Djabugay, Australia's Aboriginal people who use dance and music to share stories of their way of life.",Djabugay,Australian
2,Dance And Music Of Australian Aboriginal Djabugay People,https://culturallyours.com/2020/01/28/dance-and-music-of-australian-aboriginal-djabugay-people/,"This is the music and language of the Djabugay people, an Australian Aboriginal tribe. The Djabugay are a group of Australian Aboriginal people who are the original inhabitants of mountains, gorges, land and waters of a richly forested part of the wet tropics of Queensland including the famous Barron Gorge and its surrounding areas.",Djabugay,Australian
3,Djabugay Australian Aboriginal Dance Culture - YouTube,https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=f3SZIJ-rwsg,"A clip from a Djabugay performance of dance and music by Australia's Aboriginal people from Cairns Queensland.1) For the podcast episode about the Djabugay, ...",Djabugay,Australian
4,Australian Didgeridoo Music Culture - YouTube,https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=1Jab1GuCLEM,"Listen to the haunting and melodious music from the didgeridoo as played by the Djabugay people, one of Australia's Aboriginal people from Cairns Queensland. 1) For the podcast episode about the ...",Djabugay,Australian
5,Djabugay - About The North,https://www.aboutthenorth.au/styled-4/styled-13/styled-68/styled-194/,"Djabugay The Djabugay people (a.k.a Djabuganydji or Tjapukai) lived in the rainforest-covered mountains and gorges of the Great Dividing Range, including the Barron Gorge. Their language belongs to the Pama–Nyungan language family and is closely related to Yidin. According to Norman Tindale, their territory extended from Mareeba and Kuranda to Port Douglas and Mount Molloy, with a western ...",Djabugay,Australian
6,Djabugay Aboriginal Corporations | Kuranda QLD - Facebook,https://www.facebook.com/DjabugayAboriginalCorporations/,"Djabugay Aboriginal Corporations, Kuranda. 5,703 likes · 50 talking about this · 7 were here. Djabugay Aboriginal Corporations are now located at Nyuwarri Estate (the farm), 1496 Kennedy Hwy,...",Djabugay,Australian
7,HOME [www.djabugay.org.au],https://www.djabugay.org.au/,"In response to the Coronavirus (COVID19) pandemic, Djabugay Aboriginal Corporations temporarily closed its doors to the public from Monday 23 March 2020, and all general business, public and program activity has been put on hold. However, our staff continue to work from home, and can be contacted via mobile on: 0448 823 153 or email: info@djabugay.org.au. We hope you all continue to look out ...",Djabugay,Australian
8,Ngirrma badji! : Djabugay! / written by Bina ; illustrated by Guginy ...,https://catalogue.nla.gov.au/catalog/1133695,In Djabugay with parallel English. All songs except Djawarray (or Thunder) are available on cassette recorded by Rainbow (or Gudju-gudju). First Nations (AIATSIS) Subject: Music - Vocal Education - Language - Indigenous languages Djabugay / Tjapukai / Djabuganjdji language (Y106) (Qld SE55-01) Northeast Queensland (NE Qld SE55) Subject:,Djabugay,Australian
